    {
      "id": "note-gaps",
      "name": "Gaps",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 60],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 2300,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 5,
        "content": "## Half-Built — 3 gaps (the three substantial prompt-engineering moments of this final lab)\n\n1. **Synthesise Briefing → prompt** is blank. Write a prompt that produces an IC-style analytic briefing (150-250 words) using ONLY the sources provided. Requirements to include: cite sources via `[Source N]` markers + a Sources list at the end; use one of the seven likelihood terms (almost no chance / very unlikely / unlikely / roughly even chance / likely / very likely / almost certain); explicitly distinguish information from judgment (\"we assess\", \"the source reports\"); note one alternative hypothesis; address customer relevance. Reference sources via `{{ $json.sources.map((s, i) => '[Source ' + (i+1) + '] ' + s.title + ': ' + s.extract).join('\\n\\n') }}`.\n\n2. **Audit Briefing → prompt** is blank. Read the four files in `policies/`. Write a prompt that audits the briefing against those policies. For each violation, the auditor outputs: Citation (ICD-XXX / rule name), Severity (violation / concern / compliant), Quote, Explanation, Fix. ONLY flag issues grounded in a specific rule — do not invent rules. If clean, output exactly `COMPLIANT`. Reference the briefing via `{{ $('Synthesise Briefing').item.json.text }}` and embed the policy summaries in the prompt itself.\n\n3. **Audit Clean? → rightValue** is blank. Decide what string the IF should look for in the auditor's output to consider the briefing clean. (Hint: pick a single word that signals 'no issues found' — your auditor prompt should output that word as a discriminator.)\n\n**Rule:** no Code node. The pattern is *all four patterns combined* — Chaining, Parallel-ish (Wikipedia returns multiple hits), Routing (audit gate), Evaluator/Optimiser (revise loop)."
      }
    }
